#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
log-shape-query-plan-run - execute a log-insights query plan and report each
entry's result as it completes (log-insights skill, step 7).

The insight pass used to execute the plan itself, out of sight: the user
saw a spinner for minutes, and nobody could tell afterwards which KQL had run,
what it returned, how long it took, or whether it failed. This tool runs each
entry through clp-s-search-kql, prints one block per entry as soon as it
finishes, and records every entry in a results file that the report writer
reads instead of re-running the plan.

An entry's filter is its structured `match`, rendered to KQL by
lib/kql_build.py, so its values are quoted and its groups parenthesized by
construction. An entry without a valid `match` (a malformed filter, or a
hand-written `kql` string) is recorded as an error without running.

Usage:
  log-shape-query-plan-run [options] ARCHIVES_DIR
  log-shape-query-plan-run --print-table [--results-file F]

Options:
  --query-plan-file F   One query_plan entry per line as compact JSON
                        (default: /tmp/log-shape-query-plan.txt, written by
                        log-shape-insight-extract)
  --results-file F      Where results accumulate as NDJSON, one line per plan
                        entry (default: /tmp/log-shape-query-results.ndjson)
  --entries RANGES      1-based plan entries to run, e.g. 1-5, 7, or 1-3,9
                        (default: all). Results already recorded for other
                        entries of the same archive and plan are kept, so the
                        plan can run in batches and a single entry can be
                        re-run after a fix.
  --timeout SECONDS     Wall-clock limit per query (default: 100). A query
                        that hits it is killed and recorded as "timeout".
  --jobs N|auto         Searches to run at once. auto (default) sizes it from
                        memory, see below; N pins it (still capped at the CPU
                        count).
  --mem-per-job GIB     Assume this much memory per search and skip the
                        measurement.
  --reserve-gib GIB     Memory to leave free for everything else (default: 2).
  --max-jobs N          Upper bound for auto (default: 8).
  --retry-failed        Re-run an entry that ended in error or timeout once,
                        and mark it retried.
  --max-followups N     Cap on queries added by `then` rules (default: 20).
  --inbox F             Also take entries from F while running, and hold the
                        pool open until F says {"close": true}: each complete
                        line is a plan entry, queued AHEAD of every plan entry
                        not yet started, with origin "focus" unless it has its
                        own. log-shape-focus writes it once the user picks a
                        focus, so one pool runs the core plan and the focus
                        without a second pool counting the same free memory.
                        Its entries get indexes after the plan's last entry.
  --inbox-timeout SECONDS
                        Stop holding after this long with nothing left to run
                        and no close line (default: 900); INBOX=timed-out.

A plan entry may also carry:
  samples, sample_chars  Keep more or longer example lines for this entry.
  origin                 Free text recorded with the result (e.g. baseline).
  then                   [{"when": {"count_gt": A, "count_lte": B},
                          "run": <entry>}]: once this entry has a result whose
                         count is in that range, add the `run` entry to the
                         pool. Follow-ups get indexes after the plan's last
                         entry and origin "follow-up of N".
  --samples N           Example output lines kept per projecting entry
                        (default: 3)
  --sample-chars N      Truncate each example to N characters (default: 200)
  --search-wrapper P    Search wrapper to run (default: clp-s-search-kql next
                        to this script)
  --print-table         Print the recorded results as a Markdown table and
                        run nothing.

Methods, as defined by the classification contract (KQL is the rendered
`match`):
  count          wrapper --count ARCHIVES_DIR KQL; the per-archive counts are
                 summed.
  project+grep   wrapper --projection P ARCHIVES_DIR KQL | grep '^{'
                 [| grep -Ei GREP]; matching lines are counted.
  project+jq     wrapper --projection P ARCHIVES_DIR KQL | grep '^{'
                 | jq -c JQ; output lines are counted.
  semantic       wrapper --projection P ARCHIVES_DIR KQL | grep '^{'; the
                 match carries the semantic node itself.

Each entry gets a status: ok, zero (ran and matched nothing -- suspicious,
since every entry is derived from a template that exists), error (a stage
exited non-zero; its stderr is kept), or timeout. An entry matching at least
90% of the archive's records is also flagged non-selective: either its filter
is too broad to isolate its category, or that category makes up most of the
log -- worth a look either way.

Concurrency. A search holds its whole segment in memory (about 9 GiB for a
10 GB log), so memory, not cores, limits how many can run together. The first
search runs alone -- the total-record probe, or the first entry when the total
is already recorded -- and the runner measures its real peak resident memory.
It then starts another search only while free memory (MemAvailable, capped by
any cgroup limit) minus the room the running searches have yet to grow into,
minus --reserve-gib, still fits one more at the measured peak plus 15%. Memory
is sampled twice a second for the whole run. Should free memory drop below
1 GiB with more than one search running, the newest is stopped and requeued
(a search preempted twice runs alone). Each result records peak_rss_mb.

Stdout: TOTAL_RECORDS= (with the probe's peak memory), one block per entry as
it finishes (in completion order), PEAK_CONCURRENCY=, then a PLAN_STATUS line
(over every recorded entry, not just this run) and RESULTS_FILE=.

Exit codes: 0 the requested entries ran (failed entries are results, not
tool failures), 1 input problem.
"""

import argparse
import datetime
import json
import os
import resource
import shlex
import signal
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
import threading
import time
from concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor, as_completed

sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)), "lib"))
from kql_build import METHODS, FilterError, entry_kql  # noqa: E402

DEFAULT_QUERY_PLAN_FILE = "/tmp/log-shape-query-plan.txt"
DEFAULT_RESULTS_FILE = "/tmp/log-shape-query-results.ndjson"
NON_SELECTIVE_PCT = 90.0


def parse_ranges(spec: str, n: int) -> list:
    picked = set()
    for part in spec.split(","):
        part = part.strip()
        if not part:
            continue
        lo, sep, hi = part.partition("-")
        start = int(lo)
        end = int(hi) if sep else start
        if start < 1 or end > n or start > end:
            raise ValueError(f"entry range {part!r} is outside 1-{n}")
        picked.update(range(start, end + 1))
    return sorted(picked)


def clip_record(line: str, chars: int) -> str:
    """Shorten an over-long record by clipping its long string values, so the
    sample stays valid JSON (cutting the raw line would leave it unparseable)."""
    if len(line) <= chars:
        return line
    try:
        rec = json.loads(line)
    except json.JSONDecodeError:
        return line[:chars]
    if not isinstance(rec, dict):
        return line[:chars]
    clipped = {k: (v[:chars] + "…" if isinstance(v, str) and len(v) > chars else v)
               for k, v in rec.items()}
    return json.dumps(clipped, ensure_ascii=False)


def first_lines(data: bytes, limit: int = 5) -> str:
    lines = [ln.strip() for ln in data.decode("utf-8", "replace").splitlines() if ln.strip()]
    text = " | ".join(lines[:limit])
    return text[:500]


def run_pipeline(stages, timeout, on_line, run=None):
    """Run stages as a pipeline, feed each stdout line of the last stage to
    on_line, and return (exit codes, stderr per stage, timed_out)."""
    procs, errs = [], []
    for i, argv in enumerate(stages):
        err = tempfile.TemporaryFile()
        proc = subprocess.Popen(
            argv,
            stdin=procs[-1].stdout if procs else subprocess.DEVNULL,
            stdout=subprocess.PIPE,
            stderr=err,
            # The wrapper is a shell script that spawns clp-s; give it its own
            # process group so a timeout kills clp-s too.
            start_new_session=(i == 0),
        )
        if procs:
            procs[-1].stdout.close()
        procs.append(proc)
        errs.append(err)

    if run is not None:
        run.pgid = procs[0].pid

    timed_out = threading.Event()

    def kill_all():
        timed_out.set()
        try:
            os.killpg(procs[0].pid, signal.SIGKILL)
        except ProcessLookupError:
            pass
        for proc in procs[1:]:
            proc.kill()

    if run is not None:
        run.kill = kill_all
    timer = threading.Timer(timeout, kill_all)
    timer.start()
    try:
        for raw in procs[-1].stdout:
            on_line(raw.decode("utf-8", "replace").rstrip("\n"))
        codes = [proc.wait() for proc in procs]
    finally:
        timer.cancel()
    stderr = []
    for err in errs:
        err.seek(0)
        stderr.append(err.read())
        err.close()
    return codes, stderr, timed_out.is_set()


def count_lines_into(acc):
    def on_line(line):
        line = line.strip()
        if not line.startswith("{"):
            return
        try:
            acc["count"] += int(json.loads(line).get("count", 0))
        except (json.JSONDecodeError, TypeError, ValueError):
            pass

    return on_line


def build_stages(entry, kql, wrapper, archive):
    method = entry.get("method", "")
    if method == "count":
        return [[wrapper, "--count", archive, kql]]
    search = [wrapper]
    if entry.get("project"):
        search += ["--projection", entry["project"]]
    search += [archive, kql]
    stages = [search, ["grep", "^{"]]
    if method == "project+grep" and entry.get("grep"):
        stages.append(["grep", "-Ei", entry["grep"]])
    elif method == "project+jq":
        stages.append(["jq", "-c", entry.get("jq") or "."])
    return stages


def stage_failed(argv, code):
    # grep exits 1 when nothing matched; that is a zero result, not a failure.
    if argv[0] == "grep":
        return code >= 2
    return code != 0


def plan_kql(entry):
    """The KQL an entry runs, or None when its match does not render."""
    try:
        return entry_kql(entry)
    except FilterError:
        return None


def run_entry(entry, index, n, args, total, lines, run=None):
    method = entry.get("method", "")
    label = entry.get("label", f"entry {index}")
    lines.append(f"[{index}/{n}] {label}")

    result = {
        "index": index,
        "label": label,
        "method": method,
        "archive": args.archive,
        "total_records": total,
        "ran_at": datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat(timespec="seconds"),
    }
    for key in ("match", "project", "grep", "jq", "origin", "category", "priority", "stage"):
        if entry.get(key):
            result[key] = entry[key]

    try:
        kql = entry_kql(entry)
    except FilterError as exc:
        result.update(kql="", status="error", count=None, elapsed_s=0.0, command="",
                      error=f"invalid plan entry: {exc}")
        lines.append(f"       -> ERROR: {result['error']}")
        return result
    result["kql"] = kql
    lines.append(f"       {method or '?'}  {kql}")

    if method not in METHODS:
        result.update(status="error", count=None, elapsed_s=0.0,
                      error=f"unknown method {method!r} (expected one of {', '.join(METHODS)})")
        result["command"] = ""
        lines.append(f"       -> ERROR: {result['error']}")
        return result

    stages = build_stages(entry, kql, args.search_wrapper, args.archive)
    result["command"] = " | ".join(shlex.join(argv) for argv in stages)

    acc = {"count": 0}
    samples = []
    keep = int(entry.get("samples", args.samples))
    chars = int(entry.get("sample_chars", args.sample_chars))
    if method == "count":
        on_line = count_lines_into(acc)
    else:
        def on_line(line):
            acc["count"] += 1
            if len(samples) < keep:
                samples.append(clip_record(line, chars))

    start = time.monotonic()
    codes, stderr, timed_out = run_pipeline(stages, args.timeout, on_line, run)
    elapsed = round(time.monotonic() - start, 1)
    count = acc["count"]
    result.update(count=count, elapsed_s=elapsed)
    if run is not None and run.peak_kib:
        result["peak_rss_mb"] = run.peak_kib // 1024
    if samples:
        result["samples"] = samples

    failed = [(argv, code, err) for argv, code, err in zip(stages, codes, stderr)
              if stage_failed(argv, code)]
    if timed_out:
        result["status"] = "timeout"
        lines.append(f"       -> TIMEOUT after {args.timeout}s (partial: {count:,} rows)")
        return result
    if failed:
        argv, code, err = failed[0]
        stage = "search" if argv is stages[0] else argv[0]
        result["status"] = "error"
        result["error"] = f"{stage} exited {code}: {first_lines(err) or '(no stderr)'}"
        lines.append(f"       -> ERROR in {elapsed}s: {result['error']}")
        return result

    unit = "records" if method == "count" else "rows"
    line = f"       -> {count:,} {unit}"
    if total:
        pct = round(100.0 * count / total, 6)
        result["pct"] = pct
        line += f" ({fmt_pct(pct)} of {total:,})"
        if pct >= NON_SELECTIVE_PCT:
            result["non_selective"] = True
    line += f" in {elapsed}s"
    if count == 0:
        result["status"] = "zero"
        line += "  [ZERO: matched nothing]"
    else:
        result["status"] = "ok"
        if result.get("non_selective"):
            line += f"  [NON-SELECTIVE: >= {NON_SELECTIVE_PCT:g}% of records]"
    lines.append(line)
    for sample in samples[:3]:
        lines.append(f"          e.g. {sample}")
    return result


def mem_available_kib():
    """Memory a new process can claim: MemAvailable, capped by a cgroup limit
    (container or systemd slice) when one is set. None when neither is known."""
    avail = None
    try:
        with open("/proc/meminfo", "r", encoding="ascii") as f:
            for line in f:
                if line.startswith("MemAvailable:"):
                    avail = int(line.split()[1])
                    break
    except (OSError, ValueError, IndexError):
        pass
    for limit_file, usage_file in (
        ("/sys/fs/cgroup/memory.max", "/sys/fs/cgroup/memory.current"),
        ("/sys/fs/cgroup/memory/memory.limit_in_bytes", "/sys/fs/cgroup/memory/memory.usage_in_bytes"),
    ):
        try:
            with open(limit_file, "r", encoding="ascii") as f:
                limit = f.read().strip()
            with open(usage_file, "r", encoding="ascii") as f:
                usage = int(f.read().strip())
            if limit.isdigit() and int(limit) < (1 << 60):
                room = (int(limit) - usage) // 1024
                avail = room if avail is None else min(avail, room)
            break
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            continue
    return avail


PAGE_KIB = os.sysconf("SC_PAGE_SIZE") // 1024


def group_rss_kib(pgid):
    """Resident memory of every process in a process group (the search wrapper
    and the clp-s it spawns), read from /proc."""
    total = 0
    for name in os.listdir("/proc"):
        if not name.isdigit():
            continue
        try:
            with open(f"/proc/{name}/stat", "r", encoding="ascii", errors="replace") as f:
                fields = f.read().rsplit(")", 1)[1].split()
            if int(fields[2]) != pgid:
                continue
            with open(f"/proc/{name}/statm", "r", encoding="ascii") as f:
                total += int(f.read().split()[1]) * PAGE_KIB
        except (OSError, ValueError, IndexError):
            continue
    return total


class Run:
    """One search pipeline in flight, as the memory monitor sees it."""

    def __init__(self):
        self.pgid = None
        self.kill = None
        self.rss_kib = 0
        self.peak_kib = 0
        self.started = time.monotonic()
        self.preempted = threading.Event()

    def preempt(self):
        self.preempted.set()
        if self.kill:
            self.kill()


class Monitor(threading.Thread):
    """Samples the resident memory of every registered run twice a second, so
    the scheduler knows what a search really costs and what running ones have
    yet to grow into."""

    def __init__(self):
        super().__init__(daemon=True)
        self.runs = set()
        self.lock = threading.Lock()

    def add(self, run):
        with self.lock:
            self.runs.add(run)

    def remove(self, run):
        with self.lock:
            self.runs.discard(run)

    def run(self):
        while True:
            time.sleep(0.5)
            with self.lock:
                runs = list(self.runs)
            for r in runs:
                if r.pgid:
                    r.rss_kib = group_rss_kib(r.pgid)
                    r.peak_kib = max(r.peak_kib, r.rss_kib)


def load_results(path):
    results = {}
    try:
        with open(path, "r", encoding="utf-8") as f:
            for line in f:
                line = line.strip()
                if not line:
                    continue
                try:
                    rec = json.loads(line)
                except json.JSONDecodeError:
                    continue
                if isinstance(rec.get("index"), int):
                    results[rec["index"]] = rec
    except FileNotFoundError:
        pass
    return results


def plan_status(results, n):
    statuses = [r.get("status") for r in results.values()]
    return (
        f"PLAN_STATUS ran={len(results)}/{n} ok={statuses.count('ok')} "
        f"zero={statuses.count('zero')} error={statuses.count('error')} "
        f"timeout={statuses.count('timeout')} "
        f"non_selective={sum(1 for r in results.values() if r.get('non_selective'))}"
    )


def fmt_pct(pct: float) -> str:
    if pct == 0:
        return "0%"
    return "<0.01%" if pct < 0.01 else f"{pct:.2f}%"


def md_cell(text: str) -> str:
    return text.replace("|", "\\|").replace("\n", " ")


def print_table(results):
    if not results:
        print("(no recorded results)")
        return
    print("| # | Query | Method | KQL | Result | Time |")
    print("|---|---|---|---|---|---|")
    for index in sorted(results):
        r = results[index]
        status = r.get("status")
        count = r.get("count")
        if status == "error":
            outcome = f"**error**: {r.get('error', '')[:300]}"
        elif status == "timeout":
            outcome = f"**timeout** (partial: {count:,})"
        else:
            outcome = f"{count:,}"
            if r.get("total_records"):
                outcome += f" ({fmt_pct(100.0 * count / r['total_records'])})"
            if status == "zero":
                outcome += " **zero**"
            if r.get("non_selective"):
                outcome += " **non-selective**"
        kql = r.get("kql", "")
        label = r.get("label", "") + (" (focus)" if r.get("origin") == "focus" else "")
        print(
            f"| {index} | {md_cell(label)} | {r.get('method', '')} "
            f"| `{md_cell(kql)}` | {md_cell(outcome)} | {r.get('elapsed_s', '')}s |"
        )


def main(argv=None) -> int:
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(
        description="Execute a log-insights query plan, printing and "
        "recording each entry's result as it completes."
    )
    parser.add_argument("archive", nargs="?", help="archives directory")
    parser.add_argument("--query-plan-file", default=DEFAULT_QUERY_PLAN_FILE)
    parser.add_argument("--results-file", default=DEFAULT_RESULTS_FILE)
    parser.add_argument("--entries", default="")
    parser.add_argument("--timeout", type=int, default=100)
    parser.add_argument("--jobs", default="auto")
    parser.add_argument("--mem-per-job", type=float, default=None, metavar="GIB")
    parser.add_argument("--reserve-gib", type=float, default=2.0)
    parser.add_argument("--max-jobs", type=int, default=8)
    parser.add_argument("--retry-failed", action="store_true")
    parser.add_argument("--max-followups", type=int, default=20)
    parser.add_argument("--samples", type=int, default=3)
    parser.add_argument("--sample-chars", type=int, default=200)
    parser.add_argument(
        "--search-wrapper",
        default=os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)), "clp-s-search-kql"),
    )
    parser.add_argument("--print-table", action="store_true")
    parser.add_argument("--inbox", default=None)
    parser.add_argument("--inbox-timeout", type=int, default=900)
    args = parser.parse_args(argv)

    if args.print_table:
        print_table(load_results(args.results_file))
        return 0
    if not args.archive:
        parser.error("ARCHIVES_DIR is required unless --print-table is given")
    args.archive = os.path.abspath(args.archive)

    try:
        with open(args.query_plan_file, "r", encoding="utf-8") as f:
            plan = [json.loads(line) for line in f if line.strip()]
    except (OSError, json.JSONDecodeError) as exc:
        print(f"error: failed to read {args.query_plan_file}: {exc}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    n = len(plan)
    if n == 0:
        print(f"error: {args.query_plan_file} has no query plan entries", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    try:
        picked = parse_ranges(args.entries, n) if args.entries else list(range(1, n + 1))
    except ValueError as exc:
        print(f"error: --entries: {exc}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1

    # Keep earlier results only when they describe this archive and this plan.
    results = {
        i: r for i, r in load_results(args.results_file).items()
        if r.get("archive") == args.archive and 1 <= i <= n
        and r.get("kql") == plan_kql(plan[i - 1]) and r.get("label") == plan[i - 1].get("label")
    }

    monitor = Monitor()
    monitor.start()
    lock = threading.Lock()
    est = {"kib": int(args.mem_per_job * 1024 * 1024) if args.mem_per_job else 0}

    def calibrate(run):
        """A search that finished cleanly tells us what one costs."""
        if run.peak_kib > est["kib"] and not args.mem_per_job:
            est["kib"] = run.peak_kib

    total = next((r["total_records"] for r in results.values() if r.get("total_records")), None)
    if total is None:
        # The record count is a full search, so it doubles as the calibration probe.
        acc = {"count": 0}
        run = Run()
        monitor.add(run)
        start = time.monotonic()
        codes, stderr, timed_out = run_pipeline(
            [[args.search_wrapper, "--count", args.archive, "*"]], args.timeout, count_lines_into(acc), run
        )
        monitor.remove(run)
        elapsed = round(time.monotonic() - start, 1)
        if timed_out or codes[0] != 0:
            reason = "timeout" if timed_out else first_lines(stderr[0]) or f"exit {codes[0]}"
            print(f"TOTAL_RECORDS=unknown ({reason}; percentages omitted)", flush=True)
        else:
            total = acc["count"]
            calibrate(run)
            print(f"TOTAL_RECORDS={total} ({elapsed}s, peak {run.peak_kib / 1048576:.1f} GiB)", flush=True)
    else:
        print(f"TOTAL_RECORDS={total} (recorded)", flush=True)

    followup_budget = [args.max_followups]

    def followups(index, result):
        """An entry may carry `then` rules -- {"when": {"count_gt": A,
        "count_lte": B}, "run": <entry>} -- that add a query to the pool once
        its result is in: inspect a result as it lands and ask the next
        question while other searches still run. The budget bounds the growth."""
        count = result.get("count") or 0
        for rule in plan[index - 1].get("then", []):
            when = rule.get("when", {})
            if not (when.get("count_gt", -1) < count <= when.get("count_lte", float("inf"))):
                continue
            with lock:
                if followup_budget[0] <= 0 or not isinstance(rule.get("run"), dict):
                    continue
                followup_budget[0] -= 1
                plan.append(dict(rule["run"], origin=f"follow-up of {index}"))
                queue.append(len(plan))

    def execute(index, run):
        """Run one entry. Returns None when the memory guard preempted it."""
        lines = []
        try:
            result = run_entry(plan[index - 1], index, len(plan), args, total, lines, run)
            if (args.retry_failed and not run.preempted.is_set()
                    and result.get("status") in ("error", "timeout") and result.get("command")):
                lines.append(f"       -> {result['status']}; retrying once")
                run.pgid, run.kill = None, None
                result = run_entry(plan[index - 1], index, len(plan), args, total, lines, run)
                result["retried"] = True
        finally:
            monitor.remove(run)
        if run.preempted.is_set():
            return None
        if result.get("status") in ("ok", "zero"):
            calibrate(run)
            followups(index, result)
        with lock:
            results[index] = result
            print("\n".join(lines), flush=True)
            # Rewrite after every entry so an interrupted run keeps what finished.
            tmp = args.results_file + ".tmp"
            with open(tmp, "w", encoding="utf-8") as f:
                for i in sorted(results):
                    f.write(json.dumps(results[i], ensure_ascii=False) + "\n")
            os.replace(tmp, args.results_file)
        return result

    reserve_kib = int(args.reserve_gib * 1024 * 1024)
    hard_floor_kib = 1024 * 1024
    fixed_jobs = None if args.jobs == "auto" else max(1, int(args.jobs))
    cap = min(fixed_jobs or args.max_jobs, os.cpu_count() or 1)

    def may_start(runs):
        """Start another search only when memory can take one more. A search
        holds its segment in memory and grows into it over several seconds, so
        the room a running search has yet to fill counts as already spoken for."""
        if not runs:
            return True
        if len(runs) >= cap:
            return False
        if fixed_jobs:
            return True
        if not est["kib"]:
            return False  # nothing measured yet: stay serial
        avail = mem_available_kib()
        if avail is None:
            return False
        unfilled = sum(max(0, est["kib"] - r.rss_kib) for r in runs)
        return avail - unfilled - reserve_kib >= est["kib"] * 1.15

    queue = list(picked)
    inbox = {"offset": 0, "closed": args.inbox is None, "added": 0, "idle_since": None, "waiting": False}

    def read_inbox():
        """Queue the inbox's new complete lines ahead of the plan entries not
        yet started, in the order they were written."""
        try:
            with open(args.inbox, "rb") as f:
                f.seek(inbox["offset"])
                data = f.read()
        except FileNotFoundError:
            return
        end = data.rfind(b"\n")
        if end < 0:
            return
        inbox["offset"] += end + 1
        added = []
        for line in data[: end + 1].decode("utf-8", errors="replace").splitlines():
            line = line.strip()
            if not line:
                continue
            try:
                entry = json.loads(line)
            except json.JSONDecodeError:
                print(f"       inbox: skipped a line that is not JSON: {line[:120]}", flush=True)
                continue
            if not isinstance(entry, dict):
                continue
            if entry.get("close"):
                inbox["closed"] = True
                print(f"INBOX closed ({inbox['added']} focus entr{'y' if inbox['added'] == 1 else 'ies'})",
                      flush=True)
                continue
            with lock:
                plan.append(dict(entry, origin=entry.get("origin", "focus")))
                added.append(len(plan))
            inbox["added"] += 1
            print(f"       [{len(plan)}] queued from inbox: {entry.get('label', '')}", flush=True)
        # Ahead of the plan, behind the earlier focus entries still queued.
        ahead = [i for i in queue if i > n and plan[i - 1].get("origin") == "focus"]
        rest = [i for i in queue if i not in ahead]
        queue[:] = ahead + added + rest

    preempts = {}
    running = {}  # future -> (entry index, Run)
    peak_jobs = 0
    with ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=cap) as pool:
        while queue or running or not inbox["closed"]:
            if not inbox["closed"]:
                read_inbox()
                if not queue and not running and not inbox["closed"]:
                    now = time.monotonic()
                    if inbox["idle_since"] is None:
                        inbox["idle_since"] = now
                        print(f"INBOX waiting for the focus entries or a close line in {args.inbox}",
                              flush=True)
                    elif now - inbox["idle_since"] > args.inbox_timeout:
                        inbox["closed"] = True
                        print("INBOX=timed-out", flush=True)
                        break
                    time.sleep(0.5)
                    continue
                inbox["idle_since"] = None
            for fut in [f for f in running if f.done()]:
                index, _ = running.pop(fut)
                if fut.result() is None:  # preempted by the memory guard
                    preempts[index] = preempts.get(index, 0) + 1
                    queue.insert(0, index)
                    print(f"       [{index}] paused for memory; will retry", flush=True)
            runs = [r for _, r in running.values()]
            if queue and may_start(runs) and not (preempts.get(queue[0], 0) >= 2 and runs):
                index = queue.pop(0)
                run = Run()
                monitor.add(run)
                running[pool.submit(execute, index, run)] = (index, run)
                peak_jobs = max(peak_jobs, len(running))
                # Let it start allocating before deciding whether another fits.
                time.sleep(0.5)
                continue
            if len(runs) > 1:
                avail = mem_available_kib()
                if avail is not None and avail < hard_floor_kib:
                    newest = max(runs, key=lambda r: r.started)
                    if not newest.preempted.is_set():
                        newest.preempt()
            time.sleep(0.25)
    print(f"PEAK_CONCURRENCY={peak_jobs} (about {est['kib'] / 1048576:.1f} GiB per search)", flush=True)

    print(plan_status(results, len(plan)))
    print(f"RESULTS_FILE={args.results_file}")
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
